WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.350
On an air table, a puck glides almost
without friction towards a second puck,

2
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.600
at rest.

3
00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:09.310
They clip each other in a glancing blow.

4
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.020
Both fly away at angles,
in brand new directions.

5
00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:14.520
Directions change.

6
00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.430
Speeds change too.

7
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.780
So when two pucks collide
and fly off at angles,

8
00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.030
what exactly stays the same?

9
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:25.260
In this mission, you'll track
the momentum of each puck,

10
00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:28.940
direction and all,
before and after the hit.

11
00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:34.230
Then you'll use it to predict where the
pieces go after collisions and explosions.

12
00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:39.160
Your mission: find out exactly what stays
the same when the two pucks collide.
